  # the documented residual limit (harness doc §18.4): an IMPLICIT panic (div/0 here) has no call
  # site the checker sees, so its guarding defer does NOT run — a CONTRACT, not a gap. The
  # own-native row now asserts the SAME stderr pattern as the C route: the native backend guards
  # integer division with a compiler-organized zero check (lowered once, target-neutral, in
  # `teko::lir::lower_div_zero_guard`) that calls the SAME `tk_panic_div0` runtime helper the C
  # route's `tk_div_*`/`tk_mod_*` already call, instead of trusting an x86-64 ISA accident
  # (`idiv`/`div`'s `#DE` fault) that arm64's architecturally-defined "SDIV/UDIV by zero yields 0"
  # never shared — a PRE-EXISTING backend-parity gap found while writing this fixture, closed by
  # the fix this scenario now proves.
  Scenario: defer_implicit_panic_documented (own-native)
    Given source = "cases/defer_implicit_panic_documented.tks"
    When built and run
    Then it traps
    And stderr pattern = "teko: deliberate panic: division by zero"

  Scenario: defer_implicit_panic_documented (C route)
    Given source = "cases/defer_implicit_panic_documented.tks"
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
